    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d576">

                <pb facs="1098" n="1054" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p1/pg1054"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/8–2054: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Alger</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of State </hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d576-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-08-20T18:00:00+01:00">August 20, 1954—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>154. From Tomlinson. Limit distribution strictly. According to De Staercke, Spaak
                    and Mendes-France had sharp exchange after this morning’s session. Mendes said
                    conference would have to fail unless other countries agreed their Parliaments
                    should take some new action. Spaak said that if France insisted on this, five
                    countries would issue common declaration. Mendes angrily said it was unthinkable
                    that other western European nations emphasize divergence by isolating France in
                    such a manner.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alger</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d576-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d576-f1-content">
                <p>Sent also to Paris for Bruce and the Ambassador eyes only. Repeated to London,
                    Bonn, Rome, The Hague, and Luxembourg.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
